Second batch of android review fixes (findings #5,#6,#7,#8). Verified: cargo test -p xpressclaw-core --features android (9 pass), cargo check --workspace --features android clean + frontend build, and cargo check -p xpressclaw-server (no android) clean.

#5 fake connector test: routes/connectors.rs test_connector had '"android" => true'. The android connector already has a real validate_config (adb probe) but test_connector never called it (validate_config only runs at start via registry.start_connector_inner). Added registry::validate_connector_config(type, config) helper (public, just create_connector(type).validate_config(config).await) and an early-return in test_connector gated on #[cfg(feature=android)]. Chose android-specific early-return over routing ALL types through validate_connector_config, because the other connectors' /test intentionally only checks config shape (no network/secret probe) — changing that is scope creep. feature-off: stale android record falls to '_ => true' (nothing to probe), matching prior behavior.

#6 device-target mismatch: setup.rs check_android_sdk probed hardcoded emulator::is_running(DEFAULT_SERIAL) while /v1/android/* uses resolve_target (connector tcp/serial). Made DeviceTarget + resolve_target pub(crate) in routes/android.rs, added DeviceTarget::is_managed_emulator() and ::booted() (blocking). check_android_sdk now takes State<AppState>, resolves the SAME target in spawn_blocking, reports available=target.booted(), can_start = installed && !available && is_managed. So a BYO offline tcp device no longer shows 'Start emulator'. Also replaced the duplicated 'emulator-5554' literal at android.rs resolve_target default with emulator::DEFAULT_SERIAL. Non-android branch needs 'let _ = state;' to avoid unused-var.

#7 swallowed emulator-start errors: rewrote emulator::start. Dropped 'cmd /c start' (returned success even on emulator failure AND was the #1 injection vector) — now spawns emu binary directly on both platforms; Windows detaches via creation_flags(0x08000000) CREATE_NO_WINDOW (same pattern as tauri/src/main.rs:193 sidecar). Redirects stdout/stderr to std::env::temp_dir()/xpressclaw-emulator.log (best-effort; File::create + try_clone, fall back to null) so bad-AVD/no-accel diagnostics survive. Logs the path via tracing::info. NOTE: can't catch an emulator that spawns-then-exits (booting is async, not awaited) — but the log now captures why; #8 surfaces the timeout. Direct spawn survives parent exit on Windows (no job object set). fahreza should verify the emulator still detaches properly on their box.

#8 swallowed frontend errors: AndroidLiveView.svelte post() now checks r.ok and sets lastAction='error: <server error>' (was: lastAction pre-set to success before the fetch, 4xx/5xx ignored). startEmulator() checks r.ok, shows 'start failed', and after the 60x2s poll falls through sets 'emulator did not become reachable — check the server log' instead of silently reverting to the no-device panel.

Remaining review findings NOT yet done: #9 unclamped gesture coords (toDevice), #10 screenshot upscale guard, plus the minor ones (setTimeout not tracked in frameTimer, mcp_android.py httpx.Client per-call, ADR-024 tool count).
